<title>USA: Smith Corona seeks new hearing date.</title>
<headline>Smith Corona seeks new hearing date.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CANAAN, Conn. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Corona Corp said on Monday that it has asked the bankruptcy court for a new hearing date to confirm its reorganization plan.</p>
<p>Instead, the October 31 hearing will be used to consider the termination of the company's pension plans, a move that was previously announced.</p>
<p>Smith Corona filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy in July 1995. The company said it hopes its reorganization plan will be confirmed by the U.S. Bankruptcy Court soon.</p>
</text>
